        "title": "Carbon Cycle Geochemistry",
        "updated": "null"
      },
      "text": "The carbon cycle operates on multiple timescales simultaneously. The short cycle (biology, ocean, atmosphere) exchanges carbon in years to millennia. The long cycle (tectonics, weathering, burial) regulates CO₂ over millions of years and is the ultimate controller of Earth's climate on geological timescales."
    },
    {
      "id": "05-CARBON-CYCLE.md#003",
      "path": [
        "05-CARBON-CYCLE.md"
